From f1825e8d9584a442ff04deeff3493fb6f3341501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:45:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Refuse a milestone that changes the block time or delegate
 count

validateMergedMilestones() now refuses, at start, any milestone file
that changes the block time or the number of active delegates after
height 1. IceRoot removes the multi-span block time and delegate-count
machinery and keeps 8-second blocks with 53 validators. Solar 4.3.1
and the series without this patch load such a file and run the
multi-span code; with the refusal that code only ever sees one span.
It stays in place (crypto/src/crypto/slots.ts,
kernel/src/utils/get-blocktime-lookup.ts and the delegate-count spans
of the round calculators); the patch changes no other file.

The rule, before the checks of patches 22, 23 and 26:
- the first merged milestone (the one in force at height 1) must have
  blockTime and activeDelegates, each a positive safe integer;
- at every merged milestone, blockTime and activeDelegates must equal
  the first milestone's values (===).
The values are the numbers that JSON.parse reads from the file, so
8.0, 8e0 and 8.0000000000000001 are all the number 8 and are accepted,
and 9007199254740993 reads as 2^53 and is refused.
A refusal is InvalidMilestoneConfigurationError, "Bad milestone at
height: <h>. <key> ...", naming the height and the key. The merged
values are compared, because patch 20 changed the merge semantics: a
later milestone that restates the same number is accepted, while a
string, null or any other number is refused. Solar's own
validateMilestones() still runs first on the raw list and refuses a
delegate-count change outside a round start with its own message;
every file it refuses is refused by this rule too, so the accept set
is this rule's alone. The pool and snapshot workers feed the merged
list back to setConfig: for an accepted file that list is accepted as
well.

This is start-up validation only: every file that is accepted behaves
as before.

Also in this commit, tests of earlier patches that used a later
activeDelegates change: test 20's rank-table shrink at 107 now has
activeDelegates 51 from height 1 instead of a change to 51 at 107; test
26's accepted shrink does the same, and its "raised to 55" case becomes
activeDelegates 55 at height 1 with a 53-rank table, refused at height
1 for rank 54. Their results are as before: both pass without this
patch and fail on b45369d7 (test 20 3 of 9, test 26 34 of 44).

Checked beyond the test with this build: the mainnet and testnet
presets load, and so do the milestones of generated devnets.

Test: patches/tests/28-milestone-span-refused.test.js. Refused, naming
the height and the key: blockTime 8 then 6 at 107, then 10 at 100;
activeDelegates 53 then 51 at 107 (a round start, which Solar's own
check allows), then 55, and 51 then back to 53; a file that changes
both; a later "8", null or 53.5; both keys missing, 0, -8, 1.5, "8",
null or 2^53 at height 1; from JSON text, 9007199254740993 for either
key and activeDelegates -0 at height 1. Accepted: values restated at
107 and 213 (no next blockTime milestone is found, slot 1,000 is
8,000 s after the epoch); from JSON text, blockTime 8e0 and
activeDelegates 5.3e1 at height 1, and 8.0, 53.0 and 8.0000000000000001
restated at 107; both keys 2^53 - 1; the merged list fed back, both
presets and a generated devnet's milestones. It fails without this
patch (27 of 39) and on b45369d7 (27 of 39), and passes here. All tests
in patches/tests pass.

Patch: 28
Consensus: no
